{# Java {Bidder}BidderTest.java template — emits
src/test/java/org/prebid/server/bidder/{bidder}/{Bidder}BidderTest.java

JUnit 5 (jupiter) test class extending VertxTest. The template emits
boilerplate setUp + a baseline of canonical @Test methods that every
adapter test class needs (constructor invariants, no-content response,
malformed-response error, valid-response single-bid). Per-scenario tests
beyond the baseline are populated by the SKILL Step 5 (one @Test per
source spec's tests.fixture_inventory.exemplary[] entry; method body is
a TODO comment the operator fills using the corresponding fixture).

Inputs:
  ctx.bidder_name              : str  — Java YAML / package name (lowercase)
  ctx.bidder_class_root        : str  — PascalCase
  ctx.imp_ext_class_root       : str  — typically same as bidder_class_root
  ctx.uses_currency_conversion : bool — drives constructor signature in setUp
  ctx.has_typed_config_props   : bool — true → setUp uses the typed subclass
  ctx.endpoint_url_for_test    : str  — canonical test URL ("https://test.endpoint.com/")
  ctx.imp_ext_field_pairs      : list[dict]  — for the tiny `givenImpExt` helper;
      each {java_name: str, default_value: str (Java literal)}
  ctx.scenario_methods         : list[dict]  — per-scenario test stubs;
      each {method_name: str, summary: str (one-line // comment in body)}
  ctx.javadoc_summary          : str|null

Coverage target: ≥ 90% line-coverage on the corresponding {Bidder}Bidder.java.
Upstream asks contributors to self-certify that level (docs/developers/
contributing.md:17; the pull_request_template.md checkbox) but does not check
it — Jacoco declares prepare-agent + report only (extra/pom.xml:325-344), with
no check goal and no coverage step in pr-java-ci.yml. Measure it locally; a
green CI run says nothing about it. The template's baseline @Test set is sized
for the canonical bidder shape; bidders with extra logic (Rule 35 typed-config
branches, custom URL resolution) need additional scenario methods to reach 90%.
#}
