{# No 204 test. The Go source adapter checks http.StatusNoContent in MakeBids
    because Go hands the status to the adapter; Java does not. HttpBidderRequester
    short-circuits NO_CONTENT before makeBids is invoked (HttpBidderRequester.java
    :303 and :322 at e3ffd57), so a Java unit test feeding 204 to makeBids exercises
    the framework's contract, not the bidder's, and asserting an empty result is a
    Go semantic that cannot hold: decoding "" throws DecodeException and the bidder
    returns badServerResponse.

    Corpus: 1 of 254 upstream bidder test directories feeds 204 to makeBids
    (sparteo/SparteoBidderTest.java), and it asserts an ERROR, not an empty result,
    because SparteoBidder carries no 204 guard either. Rule 30 keeps the guard out
    of the emitted bidder; this keeps the contradicting test out of the emitted
    suite. #}
    @Test
    public void makeBidsShouldReturnErrorOnMalformedResponse() {
        final BidRequest bidRequest = givenBidRequest(identity());
        final BidderCall<BidRequest> httpCall = givenHttpCall(200, "this is not JSON");

        final Result<List<BidderBid>> result = bidder.makeBids(httpCall, bidRequest);

        assertThat(result.getValue()).isEmpty();
        assertThat(result.getErrors()).hasSize(1);
        assertThat(result.getErrors().get(0).getType()).isEqualTo(BidderError.Type.bad_server_response);
    }

    @Test
    public void makeBidsShouldReturnSingleBannerBidForCanonicalResponse() throws Exception {
        final BidRequest bidRequest = givenBidRequest(impBuilder ->
                impBuilder.id("imp-1").banner(com.iab.openrtb.request.Banner.builder().build()));
        final BidResponse bidResponse = BidResponse.builder()
                .seatbid(List.of(SeatBid.builder()
                        .bid(List.of(Bid.builder().id("bid-1").impid("imp-1").price(java.math.BigDecimal.ONE).build()))
                        .build()))
                .cur("USD")
                .build();
        final BidderCall<BidRequest> httpCall = givenHttpCall(200, mapper.writeValueAsString(bidResponse));

        final Result<List<BidderBid>> result = bidder.makeBids(httpCall, bidRequest);

        assertThat(result.getErrors()).isEmpty();
        assertThat(result.getValue())
                .hasSize(1)
                .extracting(BidderBid::getType, BidderBid::getBidCurrency)
                .containsExactly(tuple(BidType.banner, "USD"));
    }

